# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Paint Men — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for development. Set the same keys in Vercel → Settings →
# Environment Variables, or Railway → Variables.
# Every service used is free at the volumes this site will see.
#
# Everything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is inlined into the browser bundle AT BUILD
# TIME. Set it before the build that ships it — changing one later needs a
# redeploy, not just a save.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The client's details --------------------------------------------------
# These nine are what stand between this build and going live. Until they are
# set the site renders "{{PHONE}}" and friends to visitors; `npm run
# audit:content` fails while any of them is missing, so it cannot ship by
# accident. They can be set here or written straight into src/config/site.ts.

NEXT_PUBLIC_PHONE="01234 567 890"
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAIL="hello@thepaintmen.com"

# Base town, and the wider area covered. Both appear in page titles, headings
# and the structured data, so they carry real local-search weight.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TOWN="Chester"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVICE_AREA="Cheshire & North Wales"

# Years trading. A number, not a sentence — the copy reads "{YEARS} years on
# the tools".
NEXT_PUBLIC_YEARS="18"

# Whatever you would type into Google Maps to find the business. Leave unset
# and the map panel lists the towns covered instead of showing an error tile.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_ADDRESS="Chester, Cheshire"

# Social profiles. Both are already set in src/config/site.ts, so these are
# only needed to point the site at a DIFFERENT profile without a code change.
# Leave either blank and the value in site.ts is used.
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FACEBOOK_URL=

# Public site URL, no trailing slash. Canonical tags, OG images and the
# sitemap all resolve against it. Set it to the live host before launch or
# every canonical points at the default.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://thepaintmen.com

# --- Email delivery --------------------------------------------------------
# Resend — free tier covers 3,000 emails/month, 100/day. resend.com/api-keys
# Without this the quote and booking forms fail visibly and show the phone
# number instead, which is the right failure but not a shippable one.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Where enquiries and booking requests are delivered.
LEAD_TO_EMAIL=hello@thepaintmen.com

# Verified sending identity in Resend. Must be on a domain verified there.
# Falls back to Resend's onboarding@resend.dev sandbox address when unset —
# which only delivers to the Resend account owner, so it is not a launch state.
LEAD_FROM_EMAIL="The Paint Men <enquiries@thepaintmen.com>"

# --- Live chat (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Tawk.to — free plan. Dashboard → Administration → Chat Widget.
# Widget URL looks like https://embed.tawk.to/<PROPERTY_ID>/<WIDGET_ID>
# Leave both blank to disable chat entirely (no script is loaded at all).
NEXT_PUBLIC_TAWK_PROPERTY_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TAWK_WIDGET_ID=

# --- Preview mode ----------------------------------------------------------
# THE MOST IMPORTANT VARIABLE ON THIS LIST AT LAUNCH.
#
# Preview mode gates the site down to the home page, both galleries and the
# privacy notice; everything else is greyed in the menu and answers with "not
# built yet", and every page carries noindex. It is what makes the shareable
# preview for a prospect.
#
# UNSET MEANS ON. Deploy without this variable and every "Get a Free Quote"
# button lands on the not-built notice, the enquiry form is unreachable, and
# nothing is indexed — a live site that quietly collects no leads at all. The
# address bar still shows /quote, so it does not read as an outage.
#
# Set to 0 to go live. "0", "false", "off" and "no" all switch it off; any
# other value leaves it ON, so a typo fails towards showing less rather than
# publishing a half-built site.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_MODE=1

# How many "awaiting a link" placeholder cards the video gallery shows while
# there are no films in src/data/films.ts. Set to 0 to hide the gallery's empty
# state entirely once real videos arrive.
NEXT_PUBLIC_FILM_SLOTS=3
